s: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: unfriendly, unhealthy (maybe reliability). No stress info.\n\nGiven the criteria, stress resilience is crucial. C has calm in crisis. B handles stress well (our notes). D responds adequately. A unknown.\n\nDecision quality: C quick correct decisions. D solves problems extremely well. B good at assessing weather (technical). A anticipates dangerous situations.\n\nReliability: B very conscientious. C maybe reliable (not explicit but implied). D takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). A unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: C puts concern for others, positive atmosphere. B pretentious, wrong tone. D loner, moody. A unfriendly.\n\nProfessional communication: B grumpy, uncooperative. C difficulty communicating ideas. A unfriendly. D moody.\n\nOverall, C seems best balanced: strong decision, calm, attention, crew concern, despite communication difficulty.\n\nThus I will likely support Candidate C, but incorporate new evidence: stress resilience confirmed, B communication concerns, D concerns. I can argue that C remains best.\n\nMake a concise argument: I agree with Agent 1, but note B's stress handling is good but communication issues are severe; D's responsibility is good but crew cooperation lacking; A's leadership but unfriendly. Therefore C is still top.\n\nVote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
